  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_e6ece281d80f4c3c95c0fcc7311dc5fd",
      "statement": "The pipeline is orchestrated by a single sequential pass in mcp-server/src/index.ts: per-file ingest stages (loadAdoc, resolveMacros, renderAdoc, chunkPage) run in a for loop producing a flat allChunks array, then the index stages (contentHash, VectorStore.loadFromDisk or build+saveToDisk) run once, and the HTTP server starts only after the store is ready.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/index.ts#L13-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d988c3d12024b8be6e9511d00099a11bd54e4c0f9cff57990e49bb934849f3d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ada338c23b574e62ae1c0886a8341909",
      "statement": "loadAdoc recursively walks DOCS_ROOT, collecting every .adoc file into {path, relPath, raw} triples and descending into subdirectories; it skips stub files by stripping the first = heading line and dropping the file if the remaining body has fewer than 50 non-whitespace characters.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/ingest/loadAdoc.ts#L10-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0002b776e29ca7276925bd44b447f632b2d36eaa5e71b305b814609ffa060f68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_344520ff12154e4f9b0c6b11ce6dfd8f",
      "statement": "resolveMacros applies four transformations in a fixed order: Kroki/diagram blocks (matched by a regex spanning both .... and ---- delimiters and the Kroki diagram-type family) are removed entirely; include::partial$ is inlined recursively up to MAX_DEPTH=10 with nav_* partials dropped as navigation noise; include::example$ is inlined wrapped in a [source] fence; xref and image macros are reduced to their link/alt text (or dropped when empty).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/ingest/resolveMacros.ts#L1-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b8ce5452589b98bfc727c6551e1e3bc4d6fa3e69c950e87c7fe483bbad555914:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7f93aa31aec44c44b866013157a5490f",
      "statement": "renderAdoc converts preprocessed AsciiDoc to HTML via @asciidoctor/core (safe mode, standalone:false) then to plain text via html-to-text (dropping anchor hrefs and skipping img elements, since alt text was already extracted by resolveMacros); the page title is recovered from the preprocessed source's first = heading line, falling back to relPath when none is found.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/ingest/render.ts#L1-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f24472b1efacfe8051952db1734cda898022bf47fc58b7a511eda63114a392df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_38035b20303f4a19849867e71da89e8c",
      "statement": "chunkPage splits a RenderedPage into Chunks using heading detection on rendered plain text: it splits on three-or-more newlines, treats a block as a heading when it is short (<=2 lines, <100 chars, no . or ,), and falls back to a single whole-page chunk when no sections are detected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/ingest/chunk.ts#L42-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70656f553ee7624ae722ff474f2d0d85fea84e6a4c4b359f99b94014a2482435:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e3b624c74724c16b6e2292c844b567a",
      "statement": "chunkPage enforces MIN_TOKENS=80 and MAX_TOKENS=800 using an approximate token count of Math.ceil(text.length/4) (a deliberately conservative factor for Greek); sections exceeding MAX_TOKENS are split by paragraph against a budget of MAX_TOKENS minus the context prefix cost, and a merge pass folds sub-MIN_TOKENS chunks into the preceding same-page chunk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/ingest/chunk.ts#L110-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f375058c45cbfd0815f4c8ce292ed5de792c2ec0432adc91195975b28c462237:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ef4ba39ba5fa4b65a9e5212d0d7cb88b",
      "statement": "Every chunk is prefixed with a context label — either «{pageTitle}» for untitled/lead sections or «{pageTitle} › {sectionHeading}» for headed sections — so the page title and section heading are embedded into the chunk text itself for retrieval; chunk ids are ${relPath}#${slug}-${idx} where slug is the slugified heading (or page title) and idx is a per-page global counter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/ingest/chunk.ts#L113-L142",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:906e06fe5df843144a6b8e671d57d0087cac253133dd8faf6a0b094ad511f1df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e634c90cdbcd4adfac62856e915a6fbc",
      "statement": "contentHash computes a sha256 over chunk texts sorted by id and joined by null bytes, concatenated with the hardcoded PIPELINE_VERSION (1) and the embedding model name; it is computed before any embedding call so a warm cache skips the embeddings API entirely, and bumping PIPELINE_VERSION forces a re-index after ingest/chunking logic changes without editing content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/hash.ts#L1-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6f2933ee0101a12d265c132b2be2137faeb4788bbcc4399a96eabf8794e03db:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_136182b10214424dbe6cadbc8ecd362e",
      "statement": "The disk cache contract is a single JSON file per content hash: saveToDisk writes ${dataDir}/index-${hash}.json containing {hash, vectors} (mkdir recursive first); loadFromDisk reads the matching file and returns null on any read/parse error or when the stored hash does not equal the expected hash; index.ts treats null as a cache miss that triggers a rebuild and save, leaving stale files behind but ignored.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/index.ts#L37-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b53fde1c60b951dd6f7834f5143d28bb34f81f1d5e589ef613f276ed5774a3c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/store.ts#L55-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47353bacc88fc23ed24d8bb94fdced28c5d26bef3aabbdb0c3e94867e79c776e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6558a688a6db43e9880a641a858ccbc1",
      "statement": "VectorStore.build L2-normalizes each embedding to unit length at build time (passing the zero vector through unchanged), so search reduces to a linear dot-product scan of normalize(queryVec) against every stored vector, sorted descending and truncated to k; this in-memory cosine store is acceptable at the corpus scale and is the reason no external vector database is used.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/store.ts#L18-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d7162dc1c83488c794c8235e955fafe92e48dab170549ca55d0e0e3e4cf6a2b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f72fa784201a4313a89fff8cd512e587",
      "statement": "The OpenAI embedder batches inputs at BATCH_SIZE=100 per API call and wraps each call in a retry with MAX_RETRIES=3 and exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s) on HTTP 429 and status>=500, rethrowing immediately on any other status; the openai SDK is imported lazily inside embed, so a cache hit that loads vectors from disk never triggers the import or constructs a client.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/embed.ts#L10-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07ae24aa65c364812c4bd3cc8b55762fe6ba00a963237b27d9cf6d712348108f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_09a32262bc2f4b9ab9b62c69da219966",
      "statement": "A cold start that cannot reach the embeddings API fails loudly: an error from store.build propagates to main() and process.exit(1), while a warm cache hit is resilient to embeddings outages because it never calls the API; the Embedder interface ({model, dims, embed}) decouples the store, search, and cache from any vendor SDK.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/index.ts#L55-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c086d5d64b2bc144838071cb582050e93f535074ba21b52f7620f6386540f239:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/indexing/embed.ts#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87d654f1c7d01605675ac20c6bbb690e91407f8a1349003d5634801a3d8351f6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a9b12d23a1342eca660b5b63ee8ea75",
      "statement": "The vitest unit tests pin the ingest and indexing stages without a network or real API key: resolveMacros.test.ts covers every macro transformation (Kroki removal for both delimiters, partial/example inlining, nav_ skipping, xref/image replacement and drop-on-empty, recursive includes), chunk.test.ts asserts at least one chunk per page, unique ids, the page title in the context prefix, a tokensApprox<=1100 ceiling, and the ceil(len/4) consistency, and store.test.ts uses a fake embedder returning deterministic orthogonal unit vectors to prove build, cosine ranking, save/load round-trip, and null on hash mismatch or missing file.",
      "evidence": [
